k2 (done) cut the `v1` tag and changed the recommended reference in the module POD (`GETTY.pm:527,544,555,569,590`) and `.github/actions/dzil-test/README.md` to `...dzil-test@v1` (commit 391a885, 2026-09-02). No consumer followed: `grep -rhoE 'dzil-test@\S+' ~/dev/*/.github/workflows/*.yml` gives 23 references, all `@main`, none `@v1`.

Affected repos (checked 2026-10-06): p5-airlock, p5-alien-libgit2, p5-dist-zilla-plugin-licensefile, p5-git-libgit2, p5-git-native, p5-kubernetes-comb, p5-kubernetes-comb-svg, p5-net-async-authentik, p5-net-async-keycloak, p5-text-nunjucks, p5-www-authentik, p5-www-idrac, p5-www-keycloak, sick, sick-target-ciscosb, simpici.

So every change to the action still lands in all of their CI runs at once, which is what the tag was cut to stop. Decide one form and make both sides agree: either move the consumers to `@v1` (and move the tag when the action changes, see the HTTP-mirror card), or take the `@v1` recommendation back out of the POD and README.

Other things the same sweep looked at, over all 61 `p5-*` dists that use `[@Author::GETTY]`, and found in order: `.build/` and `*.tar.gz` ignored everywhere, `{{$NEXT}}` present in every `Changes`, `LICENSE` committed everywhere, `cpanfile` present everywhere. Isolated deviations only:
- build directory `Dist-Name-<version>/` not ignored: p5-www-forgejo, p5-mcp-arcraiders (their `.gitignore` has `*.tar.gz` and `.build/` but no `/WWW-Forgejo-*` / `/MCP-ArcRaiders-*` line).
- no `copyright_year` in dist.ini: p5-mcp-arcraiders. Its committed LICENSE embeds the year, so `[LicenseFile]` will abort its build from 2027-01-01 on (see the card on the LicenseFile board).
- the outdated `raudss.us` strings are already listed in k8.

